{#
  The accent palette of a landing page: `accent: { light, dark }` in the front matter of its landing file
  (`project.landing.accent`), as the inline style of the .landing wrapper. Each value becomes the custom property
  --accent-light-<key> or --accent-dark-<key>, and assets/landing.css picks the pair of the active scheme.

  The values come from another repository and go into a `style` attribute, so only the keys listed here are
  emitted, and only when the value is a hex colour (`#rgb` or `#rrggbb`). Anything else is left out and the
  default of landing.css applies; nothing else can reach the attribute. A landing without `accent` gets no style.

  Keys: accent (buttons, large accent text), accent-text (small accent text), accent-soft (tinted surfaces),
  term-accent (prompts and commands in the terminals), on-accent (text on the buttons).
#}
{% macro accentStyle(landing) -%}
{%- set keys = ['accent', 'accent-text', 'accent-soft', 'term-accent', 'on-accent'] -%}
{%- set accent = landing.accent if (landing and landing.accent is mapping) else {} -%}
{%- set declarations = [] -%}
{%- for scheme in ['light', 'dark'] -%}
{%- set values = accent[scheme] if accent[scheme] is mapping else {} -%}
{%- for key in keys -%}
{%- set value = values[key] -%}
{%- if value is string and value.match(r/^#([0-9a-fA-F]{3}|[0-9a-fA-F]{6})$/) -%}
{%- set _ = declarations.push('--accent-' + scheme + '-' + key + ':' + value) -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{- declarations.join(';') -}}
{%- endmacro %}
